.TH "SOPLOS-SYS-CLEANER" "1" "2026-10-19" "Soplos Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
soplos-sys-cleaner \- System cleaner and maintenance tool for Soplos Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soplos-sys-cleaner
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B soplos-sys-cleaner-basic
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B soplos-sys-cleaner
is the official maintenance and disk space recovery application for Soplos Linux.
Built with Tauri 2, Rust, and Svelte architecture, it provides an intuitive, high-performance interface with dry-run verification and Polkit-authenticated security:
.IP \[bu] 2
Two tailored modes: a basic one-click standard cleanup interface (\fBsoplos-sys-cleaner-basic\fR) and an advanced granular maintenance suite (\fBsoplos-sys-cleaner\fR).
.IP \[bu]
APT package cache cleaner with per-file inspection and disk space recovery.
.IP \[bu]
Old kernel and module cleaner with strict protection for active and fallback kernels.
.IP \[bu]
Unused hardware drivers and firmware cleaner with dracut and modinfo verification.
.IP \[bu]
Orphaned packages and residual configuration (dpkg state rc) purge.
.IP \[bu]
Language pack cleaner with protection for system locales.
.IP \[bu]
Flatpak runtime and Snap application leftovers removal.
.IP \[bu]
Application inventory supporting APT, Flatpak, Snap, and AppImages, with reinstall script export.
.IP \[bu]
System journal, crash dump, and temporary cache cleaner.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show summary of options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.soplos.syscleaner.policy
Polkit policy defining administrative privileges for cleanup actions.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/soplos-sys-cleaner/stats.json
User cleanup history and statistics.
